   "title": "Ex-President Yoon's senior aide gets suspended prison term over presidential residence relocation",
   "url": "https://www.koreatimes.co.kr/southkorea/society/20261127/ex-president-yoons-senior-aide-gets-suspended-prison-term-over-presidential-residence-relocation",
   "domain": "koreatimes.co.kr",
   "source": "koreatimes.co.kr",
   "published": "Fri, 27 Nov 2026 14:47:03 GMT",
   "_dt": 1795790823.0,
   "ageDays": 0.02,
   "summary": "A Seoul district court on Friday sentenced a former senior aide to former President Yoon Suk Yeol to a suspended prison term over irregularities in the 2022 relocation of the presidential residence. The Seoul Central District Court handed down a two-year prison sentence, suspended for three years, for former presidential chief of staff Kim Dae-ki after finding him guilty of abusing his power in connection with the case.",
   "summary_zh": "首尔地方法院周五就2022年总统府搬迁中的违规行为，判处韩国前总统尹锡悦的高级助理缓期徒刑。首尔中央地方法院认定前总统府首席秘书金大基滥用职权，并就相关案件判处其两年监禁、缓刑三年。",
   "summarySource": "fulltext",
   "body": "A Seoul district court on Friday sentenced a former senior aide to former President Yoon Suk Yeol to a suspended prison term over irregularities in the 2022 relocation of the presidential residence. The Seoul Central District Court handed down a two-year prison sentence, suspended for three years, for former presidential chief of staff Kim Dae-ki after finding him guilty of abusing his power in connection with the case. It also sentenced former presidential secretary for administrative affairs Yoon Jae-soon and former presidential secretary for general affairs Kim Oh-jin to one-year prison terms, both suspended for two years. The officials were indicted on charges of illegally diverting 2.09 billion won ($1.56 million) from the interior ministry's budget to pay an interior design company for the renovation of the presidential residence following its relocation from Cheong Wa Dae to the central Seoul district of Yongsan. The court found all three guilty of abusing their power by instructing officials to divert the budget, noting they were at least aware that it would be illegal to use the ministry's budget for a presidential office project. The court, however, acquitted former Interior Minister Lee Sang-min, who had also been indicted in the case, noting that his involvement was not proven. The presidential residence's move took place as part of Yoon's campaign pledge to relocate the presidential office. Incumbent President Lee Jae Myung has since moved the office back to Cheong Wa Dae. Officials have said the president and his wife are expected to move their official residence back to Cheong Wa Dae before the year's end",
