   "_dt": 1795789543.0,
   "ageDays": 0.03,
   "summary": "Namassivayam on Friday met Union Minister for Youth Affairs and Sports Mansukh Mandaviya in New Delhi. Besides being a Minister in the Prime Minister Narendra Modi-led National Democratic Alliance government at the Centre, Mr. Mandaviya was BJP’s in-charge for the April 2026 Assembly elections in the Union Territory. Mr. Namassivayam’s Office said Friday’s meeting with Mr. Mandaviya was purely to discuss official matters pertaining to the administration of Puducherry.",
   "summary_zh": "纳马西瓦亚姆周五在新德里会见了联邦青年事务与体育部长曼苏克·曼达维亚。除担任由总理纳伦德拉·莫迪领导的中央全国民主联盟政府部长外，曼达维亚先生还是人民党负责2026年4月联邦属地议会选举事务的负责人。纳马西瓦亚姆办公室表示，周五与曼达维亚先生的会面纯粹是为了讨论与本地治理由第瓦里邦行政管理有关的官方事务。",
   "summarySource": "fulltext",
   "body": "Account subscription benefits alongside Premium Stories, Editorials, Opinions and more. Unlock these with Subscription Puducherry Minister for Home and BJP leader A. Namassivayam on Friday met Union Minister for Youth Affairs and Sports Mansukh Mandaviya in New Delhi. He is also the Minister for Labour and Employment. Besides being a Minister in the Prime Minister Narendra Modi-led National Democratic Alliance government at the Centre, Mr. Mandaviya was BJP’s in-charge for the April 2026 Assembly elections in the Union Territory. Mr. Namassivayam’s Office said Friday’s meeting with Mr. Mandaviya was purely to discuss official matters pertaining to the administration of Puducherry. The Home Minister took up the Union Territory’s demand for establishing a National Centre of Excellence for sporting events, such as athletics, kabaddi, hockey, volleyball and weightlifting in Puducherry. He also briefed him about the development of sports infrastructure including synthetic athletic track and astro turf hockey field at the Indira Gandhi Sports Complex. He sought funds to the tune of ₹25 crore to distribute cash awards to meritorious sports persons pertaining to the period from 2004 to 2024. Later in the day, Mr. Namassivayam met party national general secretary (organisation) B. L. Santosh. The Minister said he discussed the current political situation in Puducherry with Mr. Santosh. Comments have to be in English, and in full sentences. They cannot be abusive or personal. Please abide by our community guidelines for posting your comments. We have migrated to a new commenting platform. If you are already a registered user of The Hindu and logged in, you may continue to engage with our articles. If you do not have an account please register and login to post comments. Users can access their older comments by logging into their accounts on Vuukle",
